  "status": "Focused qualification passed. Candidate9 full RPM and native ARM qualification remain required.",
  "root_cause": "In the offline build namespace, an unreachable DNS resolver can complete the c-ares query synchronously. Both upstream tests then inspect pending state after the request has already finished.",
  "affected_tests": [
    "test/parallel/test-dns-setserver-when-querying.js",
    "test/pummel/test-heapdump-dns.js"
  ],
  "source_review": [
    "ChannelWrap increments its active-query count before dispatch and decrements it on completion. SetServers rejects changes only while that count is nonzero.",
    "The heap snapshot expects NodeAresTask::List while c-ares sockets exist. Synchronous failure closes the sockets before the snapshot.",
    "A standalone c-ares control reproduces the same outcome for localhost and pending.example, ruling out special handling of the hostname as the cause."
  ],
  "fix": "Bind an ephemeral loopback UDP DNS fixture before starting each query. Inspect pending state synchronously, before the event loop can deliver its response. Verify the returned address, callback counts and server closure. Preserve the negative custom-resolver setServers check, successful default-resolver replacement and both ChannelWrap heap assertions.",
  "coverage": {
    "original_failures": 2,
    "fixed_javascript_runs": 42,
    "javascript_detail": "20 repeated runs of each fixed fixture, then one run of each final formatting-only revision, using the exact candidate7 binary and shared library with network=none.",
    "native_checks": 800,
    "native_detail": "100 repetitions of two hostnames with unreachable and bound-loopback resolvers, normally and under Valgrind. Verify immediate callback/no pending request for unreachable resolver; pending request and explicit cancellation for bound resolver.",
    "native_memory": "Zero errors; all 69800 allocations freed.",
    "package_checks": "Five graph-helper tests and 17 dependency preparation tests pass. All 20 candidate9 patches apply with zero fuzz; fixed DNS and raw-graph sources match the tested files byte for byte."
  },
  "prior_attempts": [
    "An initial native environment receipt queried a nonexistent development package name; no control ran.",
    "The first C control used a deprecated initialization API; the final control uses ares_init_options and compiles with -Wall -Wextra -Werror.",
    "An intermediate assertion expected identical query-return and callback status. The final control verifies the actual distinct ETIMEOUT return and ECONNREFUSED completion, with both retained in the log."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No production resolver change, timing retry, sleep or relaxed assertion.",
    "The focused tests qualify the two fixtures on Leap x86_64. The complete candidate9 build and other native architectures remain separate gates."
  ],
